<main id="main-content" class="container"><section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">About the project</div><h1>Esports365</h1><p class="lead">A student-designed esports tracking experience inspired by the convenience of mainstream scores apps, built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</p></section>
<section class="section-block grid two" id="mission"><article class="card"><h2>Problem</h2><p>Esports fans follow multiple games and teams, but match schedules, scores and streaming information can be scattered across platforms. Finding one team’s upcoming events takes time.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Our solution</h2><p>Esports365 provides a central website where visitors choose a favorite team, explore upcoming fixtures and review previous results in a clear dark-themed interface.</p></article></section>
<section class="section-block"><h2>Features</h2><ul class="about-list"><li>Team selection based on game</li><li>Dashboard featuring chosen team and recent results</li><li>Matches page with filters and demo streaming platforms</li><li>Responsive layouts and accessible form fields</li></ul></section>
<section class="section-block" id="sitemap"><h2>Site map</h2><div class="card"><p><a href="/Home">Home / Dashboard</a> → <a href="/ChooseTeam">Choose favorite team</a> → <a href="/Matches">Matches</a></p><p><a href="/">Login</a> · <a href="/SignUp">Sign Up</a> · <a href="/About">About Us</a></p><p class="small muted">Navigation is available on every page. This page also demonstrates internal navigation: <a href="#mission">Project mission</a> · <a href="#sitemap">Site map</a>.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-block"><h2>About the demo</h2><p>All fixtures and team names are illustrative. This version is a static assignment prototype, not a production application; it does not provide secure account authentication or live match feeds.</p></section></main>
